          "text": "Patient-reported gum and dental symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports hard yellow/brown material along the gums that does not come off with brushing, present for at least a few months and worsening over the last 2–3 months; gums feel puffy and bleed when brushing. No pain or toothache, ulcers, facial swelling, or difficulty eating. Partner has sometimes commented on bad breath."
      }
    },
    {
